id: pm-pmwozm
title: "Telemetry flush reliability: configurable cold-connect timeout without foreground blocking"
description: "Regression follow-up to pm-sgmb: the fixed 5-second telemetry HTTP timeout still expires on a reachable Cloudflare cold path before TLS completes, leaving privacy-safe events queued and blocking the native zero-queue assurance gate. Preserve background/non-blocking command semantics while making the worker timeout robust and testable."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: reliability,sdk,telemetry
created_at: "2026-08-13T01:23:33.814Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-13T03:25:17.594Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-13T03:25:17.124Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-13T03:25:17.124Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "A reachable slow cold connection can complete without blocking foreground commands; timeout behavior remains bounded, documented, covered at 100%, and a real local flush drains the preserved queue."
parent: pm-lnq3
repro_steps: Run pm telemetry flush against the configured endpoint on a cold route; Node fetch fails within the fixed timeout while curl eventually completes TLS to the same endpoint.
resolution: Implemented configurable cold-connect-safe native HTTP delivery plus an independent bounded deadline for replaced fetch adapters.
expected_result: Background telemetry flushes tolerate realistic cold TLS setup while foreground command latency and fail-closed assurance remain unchanged.
actual_result: "A never-settling fetch adapter times out deterministically and observes an aborted signal; live native delivery previously drained preserved events; 7,243 tests and exact coverage pass."
affected_version: 2026.8.12
fixed_version: 2026.8.13
regression: true
customer_impact: "Telemetry evidence remains queued until a later successful route, making current native health assurance fail closed."
